              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for without a break, then the Hindi for to repeat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: तैयारी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तैयारी — taiyārī — \"preparation\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अगर तैयारी अच्छी होगी तो परीक्षा से डर नहीं लगेगा। agar taiyārī acchī hogī to parīkṣā se ḍar nahīṃ lagegā. If your preparation is good, you won't be afraid of the exam."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तैयारी (taiyārī) is usually traced to Arabic tayyār, \"ready\", which reached Hindi through Persian. The Hindi noun adds the ending -ī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
